# Read by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify. Other hosts need the equivalent set in
# their own config -- these are headers a static page cannot set for itself.
#
# frame-ancestors in particular is ignored when delivered via <meta>, so this
# file is the only way to deliver it properly. main.js also refuses to run in a
# frame, so framing is blocked even on a host that ignores this.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
